    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0452" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/779.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President abdicated at three o’clock and has gone on board German war vessel
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Vineta</hi>. There was much firing and disorder but
                    the city is in charge of civil authorities who assume all responsibility. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Montana</hi> is preparing to land twenty-seven men as
                    Legation guard. <hi rendition="#italic">Vineta</hi> will do likewise.
                    Revolutionists have not yet entered city but are reported on the way from St.
                    Marco.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
